what do we need:

- content
  - about comparing bytes

- btree

- log
  - codec for WalHeader, WalEntry, and the payload

- pager
  - read
  - write
  - alloc
  - dealloc
  - set state (root, freelist, page_count)
  - read state
  - checkpoint
  - shutdown
  - buffer
    - contains page content
    - read
    - write
    - alloc
    - walk through all frames
  - evictor
    - acquired
    - released
    - evict and acquire
  - file manager
    - recover
    - spill -> move to spill buffer
    - sync -> write to file
    - get
  - log -> calling append_log
  - page -> handle operation inside a page

- recovery
  - load wal
  - iterate back for rollback (wal.rs)
  - outputs: Wal (wal.rs)
  - analyze
  - redo (recovery.rs)
  - undo (recovery.rs)
  - outputs: RecoveryResult (Wal + next txid)

- wal
  - append new
    - if it's an end transaction entry, we may be able to delete the old wal
  - flush
  - complete checkpoint
  - sync -> make sure a specific Lsn is flushed
    - used by buffer pool when they want to evict a page

- iterate wal back
  - for rollback
  - and for recovery

- stats, metrics, and logging
